  "name": "IA2 INSULING AUTOANTIBODIES",
  "code": "2024",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>IA-2 is a transmembrane protein that belongs to the protein tyrosine phosphatase family. This protein is expressed in&nbsp;human pancreatic islet cells.</p>\n<p><br>Positive IA2- Insulin indicates the risk of developing Type 1 Diabetes and future need for Insulin therapy in diabetes&nbsp;patients.</p>\n<p>IA2-antibodies are detected in approximately 60% individuals with new onset type 1 DM.</p>\n<p><strong>Clinical Utility:</strong></p>\n<p><br>These antibodies can be used to predict the onset of diabetes mellitus. In the assessment of first degree relatives for&nbsp;autoimmune diabetes, positive results in more than one of the marker antibodies (GAD, Islet cell, IA2 or insulin) can&nbsp;be associated with the onset of autoimmune diabetes</p>\n<p>Note:</p>\n<p>Patient samples containing human anti mouse antibodies (HAMA) may give falsely elevated or decreased values.<br><strong>Associated Tests:</strong><br>Insulin Antibody(I0276), Anti GAD 65 (G0058), Islet cell Antibody (I0287), Zinc Transporter 8 (ZnT8) Antibody (Z0015)&nbsp;Reference:</p>\n<p>Kit Insert<br>Belhiba O, Aadam Z, Jeddane L, Saile R, Salih Alj H, Bousfiha AA, Jennane F. Research of anti-GAD and anti-IA2&nbsp;autoantibodies by ELISA test in a series of Moroccan pediatric patients with diabetes type 1. Afr Health Sci. 2020&nbsp;Sep;20 (3):1337-1343.</p>",
